From ef17857c551b427ccf85c75424a42c8952edb187 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 18:58:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] camera: a 1.85:1 size follows the height the driver has

Why:
The port rewrote 3840x2076 / 1920x1038 to 3840x2072 / 1920x1036 on every
load, save, set_resolution, preset and ladder rung
(migratedImx585CropResolution). That works only with the cinemate-port
imx585 driver; the original Apertar driver has 2076 / 1038, so a stock
camera asked for a size its driver does not have, and every saved file was
changed on load. Original Apertar maps a size a client sends to the
sensor's own size in the per-sensor normaliser, at use, and never rewrites
the saved value on load (isImx585LowResolutionAlias and
normalizedResolutionForSensor, CameraController.cpp@upstream-1.6.0).

What:
Imx585Modes.hpp gains driverCropSize(): for a 1.85:1 size it returns the
height of the pair that the startup probe found in the class (bit depth,
Clear HDR); with nothing probed, the request if the class has it, else its
partner. Other sizes come back unchanged. CameraController calls it in
imx585ModeForResolution (the sanitiser's IMX585 step and the mode
selection) and in setResolution's class check. The rewrite on load, in
setResolution and in presets is gone. Ladder rungs follow the driver
through followDriverCropSizes, in set_mode_ladder and in start() after the
session start ran the probe (it was in the constructor, before the probe).
isImx585LegacyCropResolution lists 2076 and 1038 again, so every sensor's
validator accepts them, as in 1.6.0. The WebUI drops its 2076->2072 and
1038->1036 aliases and shows what Core reports.

Tested:
check_core.sh both tests: both builds, 18 host tests pass;
imx585_modes_test has driverCropSize cases for the port driver's and the
original driver's size sets, an empty probe, H12 and H16.
--simulate (sensor Unknown): set_resolution 3840x2076 -> get_state
3840x2076, camera_settings.conf keeps resolution_height=2076 after a
restart; 3840x2072 and 1920x1038 round-trip; the WebUI page loads without
script errors and imx585NormalizedResolution keeps 3840x2076.
Needs the camera, port driver: a camera_settings.conf with
resolution_height=2076 starts at 3840x2072
(journalctl -u apertar-core -b | grep 'camera configured'); a ladder with a
3840x2076 rung shows it as 3840x2072 and valid in get_mode_ladder before
and after a restart. Original driver (after the readout check commit):
set_resolution 3840x2076 configures raw 3840x2076.

